#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096382 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "739b1cbc-c1a7-547d-a9fb-1f244bd36827" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/id #uuid "b77c065c-3821-513c-9376-6e7108074616" :question/math-academy-id "e-4701" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$x - y + z = 1; y + z =-2; - x + 2y + z =-1$.\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nM\\begin{vmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & R_{3}\\end{vmatrix}:=R_{3} + R_{1}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{3} \\mid:=R_{3} + (-1)R_{2}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\nx - y + z = 1; y + z =-2; z = 2\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $z=2$ tells us the value of $z$. Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny + (2) =-2⟹y =-4\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting both $y=-4$ and $z=2$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx - (-4) + (2) = 1⟹x =-5\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-5$, $y=-4$, and $z=2$. Or, in vector form, $\\langle -5,-4,2 \\rangle$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096383 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd47a43f-1e99-5909-aa48-da8690025197" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination with Row Exchanges"}] :question/id #uuid "7760b6ce-91fb-5ba6-beb2-c244d6a73d69" :question/math-academy-id "e-4702" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n$x + y + z =-2; x + y + 2z =-1; x + 2y + z = 1$.\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nM\\begin{vmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & R_{2}\\end{vmatrix}:=R_{2} + (-1)R_{1}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{3} \\mid:=R_{3} + (-1)R_{1}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNote that we get $a_{22}=0$. Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n$M\\begin{vmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & R_{2}\\end{vmatrix}↔R_{3}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\nx + y + z =-2; y = 3; z = 1\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=1$ tells us the value of $z$, and the second equation $y=3$ tells us the value of $y$. Substituting these values into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx + (3) + (1) =-2⟹x =-6\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-6$, $y=3$, and $z=1$. Or, in vector form, $\\langle -6,3,1 \\rangle$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097101 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "739b1cbc-c1a7-547d-a9fb-1f244bd36827" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9206da9d-4654-5413-b740-0976d8d72e82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095013} {:answer/id #uuid "dc537d63-70d8-53aa-9da4-af806fee5d6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095014} {:answer/id #uuid "ffcd3ec7-92ad-50dd-9850-c9736427f688" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095015} {:answer/id #uuid "0a02dd75-1a7e-59af-8b97-9c352b16b1a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -10 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095016} {:answer/id #uuid "0cc1b82d-6f9b-584b-b08a-bb7df39d6ea6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095017}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9206da9d-4654-5413-b740-0976d8d72e82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095013} :answer-field/id #uuid "288bb38c-2530-527a-b84e-ca4ed7e2bd64" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095012}] :question/id #uuid "a19bbe50-faec-58bf-b57a-44ae8f766527" :question/math-academy-id "q-20505" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n${x + 2y + 6z = 5; y - 10z =-11; 4x + 8y + 13z = 9$\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097269 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd47a43f-1e99-5909-aa48-da8690025197" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination with Row Exchanges"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab1df4f7-b683-58f9-9a53-9ab3b8f3de6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x = 4$, $y = 5$, and $z = 2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095972} {:answer/id #uuid "d48de23d-197f-5638-8f67-022bd20311ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x = 4$, $y =-5$, and $z = 2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095973} {:answer/id #uuid "ef4aec20-6490-5d49-b934-a54e24f45880" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x = 4$, $y = 6$, and $z = 5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095974} {:answer/id #uuid "f5b2100b-3e34-5897-a886-74eaa7dc84ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x =-1$, $y = 2$, and $z = 5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095975} {:answer/id #uuid "3759267e-7f9c-5109-a8da-b96bba06dc96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x = 1$, $y =-6$, and $z =-5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095976}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef4aec20-6490-5d49-b934-a54e24f45880" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x = 4$, $y = 6$, and $z = 5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095974} :answer-field/id #uuid "a873c750-ef0d-5d9f-b3a2-06f31ec27870" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095971}] :question/id #uuid "cdba1d21-3eaf-575a-9b38-07c8181fcd34" :question/math-academy-id "q-73396" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n${x - y + 2z = 8; - 2x + 2y - 3z =-11; x + z = 9$.\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system."}]}
